WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.010
- [Instructor] Katie
throws a ball in the air

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:03.910
for her dog to chase.

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:08.260
The function f models the
height of the ball, in meters,

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.870
as a function of time, in
seconds, after Katie threw it.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.620
And we could see that right over here.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.230
This is our function f.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.390
So at time t equals zero,

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.760
the height looks like
it's a couple of meters.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.880
And then as we go forward in time,

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.180
to a little under 2 1/2
seconds, the ball's going up.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.700
And then after a little
under 2 1/2 seconds,

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.420
the ball starts going down.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.140
And after, by the time you get

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.760
to five seconds or close to five seconds,

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.600
it looks like the ball is on the ground.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.070
Its height is zero meters.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.510
So then they ask us

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.640
which of these statements are true?

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.350
Choose all that apply.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:47.643
So pause this video, and
see if you can work it out.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.680
All right, now let's
look through the choices.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.680
So the first one says Katie threw the ball

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.260
from a height of five meters.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.910
So let's see if that bears fruit

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.310
or (chuckles) see if that's true.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.360
So if she threw it from
a height of five meters,

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.040
that means that the y-intercept

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.230
would've been at five meters.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.260
At time t equals zero,

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.990
we would've been at a
height of five meters.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.690
Clearly, that is not the y-intercept.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:09.920
It looks like she threw it from a height

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.910
of maybe 1 1/2 or two meters.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:15.050
So I'm assuming that Katie
is not five meters tall.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.430
So she wasn't on a ladder or anything.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.260
She just threw it from her regular height.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.370
And so we can rule out this first choice.

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:24.640
The second one says at its highest point,

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.560
the ball was about 31
meters above the ground.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.530
Let's see if that is true.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.810
So the highest point is right over here.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:36.570
And yeah, that looks about 31 meters,

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.460
so I like that choice.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.623
So I will select that one.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:45.420
The ball was in the air
for about 2 1/2 seconds.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.130
So we can clearly see
that that is not the case.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.500
The ball was going up

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.830
for about 2 1/2 seconds,
but then it was going down

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:55.280
for roughly another 2 1/2 seconds.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.760
And so it was actually in the
air for almost five seconds.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:03.083
So I would rule this one out.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.250
The ball reached its
highest point in the air

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.600
about 2 1/2 seconds after Katie threw it.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.270
So let's see, after Katie,

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.430
2 1/2 seconds after Katie threw the ball,

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.600
it's right over there.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.210
It looks like it reached its highest point

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.410
a little bit before that.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:22.420
But they said about, so they're
speaking in rough terms.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.320
So I think that statement can be true.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.780
It's about 2 1/2 seconds.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.340
If they said exactly 2 1/2 seconds,

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.390
I wouldn't have selected it
'cause it seems like it happened

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:33.070
at like 2.45 seconds
or something like that.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:36.293
But there you go, those are
the ones that seem true.

